mp3val
------------------------------------------
MP3val is a small, high-speed, free software tool for checking MPEG audio
files' integrity. It can be useful for finding corrupted files (e.g.
incompletely downloaded, truncated, containing garbage). MP3val is also able to
fix most of the problems. Being a multiplatform application, MP3val can be
runned both under Windows and under Linux (or BSD).

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1

Canonical website:
  https://sourceforge.net/projects/mp3val/

Canonical download:
  mirror://sourceforge/mp3val/mp3val-0.1.8-src.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack mp3val-0.1.8-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./mp3val-0.1.8-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/mp3val-0.1.8-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/mp3val-0.1.8-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(mp3val)
  /usr/bin/mp3val.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/mp3val.README
  /usr/share/doc/mp3val/COPYING
  /usr/share/doc/mp3val/changelog.txt
  /usr/share/doc/mp3val/html/manual.html
  /usr/share/man/man1/mp3val.1.gz

